## ⏱ Time and Space Complexity

| Metric            | Complexity |
|-------------------|------------|
| Time Complexity   | `O(log n)` — proportional to the number of bits in `n` |
| Space Complexity  | `O(1)` — only a few variables |

---

## 🎯 Final Thoughts
This solution is efficient because it processes the binary representation of `n` directly using bitwise operations. It avoids converting to a string and instead leverages shifting (`n >>= 1`) for speed. The logic is clean and ensures early updates to the maximum gap as soon as new `1`s are found.  

